# Review ownership.
#
# The design-system maintainers own everything that reaches a customer: the
# published packages, the registry source, the tokens, and the pipeline that
# generates the rest. A change to any of those is an API change whether or not
# it looks like one.
#
# Owners are named individually. `zoworkhq` is a personal account, not an
# organisation, so it cannot have teams. This file used to name
# `@zoworkhq/zoblocks-maintainers`, and GitHub reported every rule as "Unknown
# owner" and silently requested no reviews at all. After editing this file,
# check it with:
#
#   gh api repos/zoworkhq/zoblocks/codeowners/errors
#
# An empty `errors` list is the only proof that it works. Every owner needs
# write access to the repository.
#
# Approval from any one listed owner satisfies a rule. Nobody can approve their
# own pull request, so a change by one maintainer is reviewed by the other.
#
# The last matching rule wins, so the specific rules below must repeat the full
# owner list. They exist so that narrowing ownership of one area later is a
# one-line change that cannot quietly drop the rest.

*                               @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan

# Shipped source — always a maintainer review.
/packages/                      @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/registry/                      @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan

# The generator decides what the registry, the docs, and the type paths contain.
/scripts/gen/                   @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan

# Architecture invariants and the contribution standard.
/ENGINEERING.md                 @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/ARCHITECTURE.md                @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/CONTENT.md                     @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/content/decisions/             @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan

# Supply chain and release. A change here changes what ships and who can ship
# it — including this file, which decides who reviews everything else.
/.github/                       @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/.changeset/config.json         @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/package.json                   @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/pnpm-workspace.yaml            @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/pnpm-lock.yaml                 @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
/SECURITY.md                    @arnabdas @rahulrajeevan
